This project runs Kokoro-82M by hexgrad (https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro,
https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
No model weights are included here: build/ downloads kokoro-onnx's ONNX export of
Kokoro-82M and cuts and rewrites it into the graphs this project runs.

Parts of build/surgery.py are adapted from build.py in kokoro-server by marty1885
(https://github.com/marty1885/kokoro-server): the rewrite of the stride-10
ConvTranspose as zero-interleave plus a stride-1 convolution, and the clipped
polynomial Sin (kept only to reproduce kokoro-server's NPU build in the
evaluation). Its notes also showed that GlobalAveragePool keeps the normalisation
on the NPU and that Snake's 1/alpha can be folded into the next convolution. These
parts were modified for this project. kokoro-server had no license file when this
was written; much of it derives from Kokoro, so we treat what we adapted from it
as carrying Kokoro's Apache License 2.0 terms.

At run time it uses kokoro-onnx by thewh1teagle (https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx,
MIT License), onnxruntime, and Rockchip's RKNN runtime (librknnrt); the NPU graphs
are compiled with Rockchip's rknn-toolkit2 (https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-toolkit2).
